## The Markup and CalMatters

Data from The Markup and CalMatters investigation "We caught companies making it harder to delete your personal data online" is licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

- Dataset: https://github.com/the-markup/investigation-data-broker-opt-out-pages
- License: https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

Rows whose `sources` value includes `markup` use URLs from that dataset. Changes were made, including which URL was kept when a company published more than one and the notes written for this catalog.

## California Privacy Protection Agency

Rows whose `sources` value includes `cppa` use the privacy-rights URL a data broker submitted in the California Data Broker Registry published by the California Privacy Protection Agency.

- Registry: https://www.cppa.ca.gov/data_broker_registry/

The registry page is a government publication. Notes in this catalog were written for this list.

## Company sites and official choice pages

Some `manual` rows are official consumer tools recorded from the publisher, including the FTC Do Not Call Registry, DMAChoice, the Digital Advertising Alliance, and California DROP. Further `manual` rows were taken from each company's own opt-out or privacy page, and from these official choice pages:

- YourOnlineChoices, the European Interactive Digital Advertising Alliance choice site: https://www.youronlinechoices.com/uk/your-ad-choices
- YourAdChoices Canada, the Digital Advertising Alliance of Canada: https://www.youradchoices.ca/choices
- Network Advertising Initiative opt-out instructions: https://thenai.org/how-to-opt-out/
- Canada's National Do Not Call List (CRTC): https://www.lnnte-dncl.gc.ca/en/
- UK open electoral register (GOV.UK): https://www.gov.uk/electoral-register/opt-out-of-the-open-register

Further `manual` rows are Canadian official pages, including Canada Post advertising-mail choices, the Canadian Marketing Association Do Not Mail service, Elections Canada and provincial voters-list pages, and privacy-commissioner guidance or complaint forms:

- Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada: https://www.priv.gc.ca/en/privacy-topics/information-and-advice-for-individuals/your-privacy-rights/raise-privacy-concern/
- Office of the Information and Privacy Commissioner for British Columbia: https://www.oipc.bc.ca/forms/individuals/complaints/
- Office of the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Alberta: https://oipc.ab.ca/privacy-correction-complaint
- Commission d'acces a l'information du Quebec: https://formulaire.cai.gouv.qc.ca/

Those pages belong to their publishers. This repository stores the link, a category, and a short note.

